// KCoreUI's test suite, in the Foundation `Test`-construct shape.
//
// Every case drives the public API: records through the writer, bytes through
// the parser, names through the resolver. Nothing reaches inside a catalog to
// assert on a field the format does not expose, because a test that does that
// stops proving the format works and starts proving it has not changed.
//
//   kira test --backend vm tests/kcoreui_kik
//   kira test --backend llvm tests/kcoreui_kik
//
// Both backends must agree. The framework is ordinary Kira and a catalog that
// resolves differently under interpretation than under compilation is exactly
// the class of bug the deterministic specificity rule exists to make impossible.
//
// The runner expands into this file, so what it calls has to be in scope here.
import Foundation
import KCoreUI
